<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>Confessional Reformed And Baptist Churches Map</name>
    <description><![CDATA[====== HOW TO USE ======<br>Click the Down Arrows (looks like a v) for more info.<br>- Zoom down into the map to see individual churches in your country/state/city. Click + button, or roll the mouse to zoom in.<br>- Or type your desired city, state into the search bar and then use your mouse to zoom into the area you where you want to find a church<br>- A list of churches with unique icons should be visible on the left of the map. You can check or uncheck groups to make them appear/disappear from the map. Ex: Uncheck PCA churches. Or uncheck 1689 London Baptist churches. <br>- Google maps on the cell phone is more limited than the computer, so it may not show the ledger on the left of the map<br><br>*** To make suggests and requests, scroll to bottom and email me ***<br><br>Last Updated March 2026<br>Updated 10/14/24<br>Updated 10/12/24<br>Updated 10/9/2024 <br>Updated 10/8/2024 <br><br>====DISCERN CHURCHES====<br>BAD THEOLOGY. Discern churches which may claim Confessionalism but have moved in a liberal direction and also churches without pastoral accountability or oversight (one-man-shows). It is argued that denominations tend to provide greater accountability against rogue pastors and greater adherence to the Confessions. Also discern pastors who preach Federal Vision theology. <br><br>ABUSE ACCUSATIONS: Due to the continued failure of churches to properly protect those who have been sexually, physically and emotionally abused, it seemed necessary to add markers ("skull and crossbones") in TOWN CENTERS where accusations have been made. Since the churches/denoms did not rule anyone guilty, the churches/pastors will remain unnamed in the header but link listed under Notes. Thus, church seekers should be cautious of churches in towns with these "skull and crossbones" markers. The church itself may NOT be on this map but the pastors may do work at churches or seminaries on this map.<br><br>--- NAPARC denominations ---<br>The Associate Reformed Presbyterian Church (ARPC)<br>The Canadian Reformed Churches (CanRC)<br>The Reformed Church of Quebec (ERQ)<br>The Free Reformed Churches of North America (FRCNA)<br>The Heritage Reformed Congregations (HRC)<br>The Korean American Presbyterian Church (KAPC)<br>The Korean Presbyterian Church in America (Kosin) (KPCA)<br>The Orthodox Presbyterian Church (OPC)<br>The Presbyterian Church in America (PCA)<br>The Presbyterian Reformed Church (PRC/PresRC)<br>The Reformed Church in the United States (RCUS)<br>The Reformed Presbyterian Church of North America (RPCNA)<br>The United Reformed Churches in North America (URCNA)<br><br>--- Confessional Denominations Outside of NAPARC ---<br>Free Church of Scotland Continuing (FCC)<br>Protestant Reformed Churches of America (PRCA)<br>Free Presbyterian Church of Scotland (FPCS)<br>Free Presbyterian Church of North America (FPCNA)<br>AND MANY OTHERS<br><br>--- Other Non-Denom churches holding strictly to the Westminster Standards and 3 Forms of Unity<br><br>--- 1689 London Baptist Confessional Churches ---<br><br>**** A special BIGGEST thanks to Ross Brunner who built the original NAPARC map, which this the basis for this map. ****<br><br>* Please understand that no one knows ALL the Confessional churches on earth, so your own church is not intentionally left off. Simply put in a request to have your church added. (See below)<br>** Currently adding more ARBCA and Korean churches; Need more strict Reformed Anglican and strict LBC 1689 Baptist churches to let us know they exist. Also STRICT Confessional churches around the world are needed with precise meeting location information. (Contact me below)<br><br>****** TO MAKE SUGGESTIONS ******<br>Please *politely* Facebook Private Message (PM) "Psyche Joy Lee" or email psychejoylee@gmail.com <br>Please include ALL the following info: <br>1) Church name:<br>2) MEETING address/Location (not mailing address). Specify if meeting in someone else's building:<br>3) Confessions (Strict WStds, 3FU, LBC). Please be honest and open. If your church is not "full subscriptionists" or takes exceptions, please specify. It does NOT mean your church won't make the map (many are already listed on the map):<br>4) Denomination/Association:<br>5) Website, pastor name, worship times, sermon audio link or any other info you want posted:<br><br>****DO NOT comment on a FB thread because FB doesn't notify me often and I will likely never see your comment.]]></description>
