      <Placemark>
        <name>New City Fellowship</name>
        <address>New City Fellowship Orthodox Presbyterian Church</address>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AL_Y2X7Z2CiFaXC1YcvZWyCfQIXF-uSN35zq7YI4ytrZFD7M5Nku9ddFG6LwIG3UujFiXkIvHRgeLZ8f6_A85tJD4OTtBDsro8tb0nZBK5AA3xBLfzJrX4r-zBw7JOoQMKymEt7ZbcY5vt1eqBR6lykg7XRtTzefYGHMC2DdIs2qZQJr1TKopvuEBKgPvS5OAoG9H85YnNo?fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>City: <br>Location: <br>Location (Addresses): <br>Contact: Email: edmondson.1@opc.org Phone: 616-427-3088<br>Denomination: Orthodox Presbyterian Church<br>Presbytery: <br>Ministry Emphases: Social Justice; Cross Cultural; Multicultural<br>Pastor: Mika Edmondson is the pastor of New City Fellowship OPC, a "cross-cultural" church plant in Southeast Grand Rapids. He graduated from Calvin Seminary, where he wrote a dissertation on Martin Luther King Jr.'s theology of suffering - "The Power of Unearned Suffering: The Roots and Implications of Martin Luther King, Jr.’s Theodicy." Mika has written for the Gospel Coalition and is a member of African American Ministries: https://aampca.org/person/mika-edmondson/<br>Worship Times: <br>Website: www.newcitygr.org<br>Leadership: http://www.newcitygr.org/about-1<br>Sermons: <br>Social Media: https://twitter.com/mika_edmondson Mika talks about “The Real MLK.” https://t.co/5aIMyDYbbM?amp=1<br>Notes: Cross Cultural/Multicultural: "the kingdom of God has always been a multicultural kingdom…”<br><br>New City Fellowship is a biblically Reformed church, planted in the spring of 2014 by Harvest Orthodox Presbyterian Church. NCF became a particular congregation of the OPC in June 2017. Our location near the corner of Burton and Eastern allows us to serve three converging cultures: white communities to the south, black neighborhoods to the north, and a quickly increasing number of Latino people to the west.<br>]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1669-DB4436</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="City">
            <value/>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Location">
            <value/>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Location (Addresses)">
            <value/>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Contact">
            <value>Email: edmondson.1@opc.org Phone: 616-427-3088</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Denomination">
            <value>Orthodox Presbyterian Church</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Presbytery">
            <value/>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Ministry Emphases">
            <value>Social Justice; Cross Cultural; Multicultural</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Pastor">
            <value><![CDATA[Mika Edmondson is the pastor of New City Fellowship OPC, a "cross-cultural" church plant in Southeast Grand Rapids. He graduated from Calvin Seminary, where he wrote a dissertation on Martin Luther King Jr.'s theology of suffering - "The Power of Unearned Suffering: The Roots and Implications of Martin Luther King, Jr.’s Theodicy." Mika has written for the Gospel Coalition and is a member of African American Ministries: https://aampca.org/person/mika-edmondson/]]></value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Worship Times">
            <value/>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Website">
            <value>www.newcitygr.org
Leadership: http://www.newcitygr.org/about-1</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Sermons">
            <value/>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Social Media">
            <value>https://twitter.com/mika_edmondson Mika talks about “The Real MLK.” https://t.co/5aIMyDYbbM?amp=1</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Notes">
            <value><![CDATA[Cross Cultural/Multicultural: "the kingdom of God has always been a multicultural kingdom…”

New City Fellowship is a biblically Reformed church, planted in the spring of 2014 by Harvest Orthodox Presbyterian Church. NCF became a particular congregation of the OPC in June 2017. Our location near the corner of Burton and Eastern allows us to serve three converging cultures: white communities to the south, black neighborhoods to the north, and a quickly increasing number of Latino people to the west.
]]></value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="gx_media_links">
            <value>https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AL_Y2X7Z2CiFaXC1YcvZWyCfQIXF-uSN35zq7YI4ytrZFD7M5Nku9ddFG6LwIG3UujFiXkIvHRgeLZ8f6_A85tJD4OTtBDsro8tb0nZBK5AA3xBLfzJrX4r-zBw7JOoQMKymEt7ZbcY5vt1eqBR6lykg7XRtTzefYGHMC2DdIs2qZQJr1TKopvuEBKgPvS5OAoG9H85YnNo?fife=s16383</value>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
