      <Placemark>
        <name><![CDATA[Solomon's Porch Christian Community]]></name>
        <description><![CDATA[Denomination: SBC<br>Confessionalism: The elders must ascribe to one of the major reformed confessions (our constitution lists Westminster, 2nd London Baptist, Savoy Declaration, or Belgic Confession). As you can probably guess, we are a mixed body of paedo and credo baptists; we accept both and desire to have a body that can have both. Members of the church must ascribe to at least the Nicene Creed. <br>Street Address: <br>City: <br>State: <br>Country: <br>Location: We meet at Stewartsboro Elementary School on Sunday mornings. 10479 Old Nashville Hwy Smyrna, TN 37167<br>Service Times: 10:10 AM - Community Education and Children's Catechism <br>This is a time before the service where the church gets together to discuss a book, a series, etc. together, as well as a time for our pastor to lead a catechism class for children 12 and under. <br><br>11 AM - Community Worship<br>This gathering always includes four elements. The preaching and teaching of God’s Word, the taking of the Lord’s Table, sharing a common meal, and offering prayer and praise. We call these elements the Four T’s.<br><br>Truth (Apostles Doctrine)<br>Together (Fellowship)<br>Table (Breaking of Bread)<br>Throne (Prayer)<br>Phone: <br>Pastor Name(s): Jeremy Mack<br>Website: https://thesolomonsporchnashville.com/ <br>Sermons: https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCFNGdNiZhNO7jaLhaWsNGug/videos<br>Email: <br>Social Media: <br>Notes: ]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1697-DB4436</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Denomination">
            <value>SBC</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Confessionalism">
            <value>The elders must ascribe to one of the major reformed confessions (our constitution lists Westminster, 2nd London Baptist, Savoy Declaration, or Belgic Confession). As you can probably guess, we are a mixed body of paedo and credo baptists; we accept both and desire to have a body that can have both. Members of the church must ascribe to at least the Nicene Creed. </value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Street Address">
            <value/>
          </Data>
          <Data name="City">
            <value/>
          </Data>
          <Data name="State">
            <value/>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Country">
            <value/>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Location">
            <value>We meet at Stewartsboro Elementary School on Sunday mornings. 10479 Old Nashville Hwy Smyrna, TN 37167</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Service Times">
            <value><![CDATA[10:10 AM - Community Education and Children's Catechism 
This is a time before the service where the church gets together to discuss a book, a series, etc. together, as well as a time for our pastor to lead a catechism class for children 12 and under. 

11 AM - Community Worship
This gathering always includes four elements. The preaching and teaching of God’s Word, the taking of the Lord’s Table, sharing a common meal, and offering prayer and praise. We call these elements the Four T’s.

Truth (Apostles Doctrine)
Together (Fellowship)
Table (Breaking of Bread)
Throne (Prayer)]]></value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Phone">
            <value/>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Pastor Name(s)">
            <value>Jeremy Mack</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Website">
            <value>https://thesolomonsporchnashville.com/ </value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Sermons">
            <value>https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCFNGdNiZhNO7jaLhaWsNGug/videos</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Email">
            <value/>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Social Media">
            <value/>
          </Data>
