      <Placemark>
        <name><![CDATA[Chiesa Cristiana Evangelica "Sola Grazia"]]></name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AL_Y2X58usDJzCUewYa-WpO82nGNItALhZDOtVf5RLB8V6hf0a7Wib04i6Y73CYZo2MRh3gdJC3iGNrnVLGDFf3T0D6JBqSGX_OuMDVmx1YJCbFcmA9mnq4CrWxjEgVRcMHatnetkqeYY3jBVY6DfKb7N4ofz_LhhAlOkdKLaJikCqhVvbqR1sSRTNrITzQSVjoC3BTpNI0?fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Denomination: Non-Denom<br>Confessionalism: 1. The Baptist Confession of Faith of 1689<br>The Evangelical Christian Church Sola Grazia is a "confessional church". This means that it goes back and recognizes itself in historical Christianity which was expressed by compiling those compendia of the evangelical faith that flourished in the 16th and 17th centuries. In particular, the "Baptist Confession of Faith of 1689" (CFB1689) is the one that, in our opinion, better than all the others, contains the essence of biblical faith.<br><br>It is and remains a human and therefore fallible document. A document that was affected by the bitter polemics and theological discussions of its time and, therefore, more capable of responding to questions that we, today, would not put "on the agenda". Finally, being an "ancient" document, it is necessarily incomplete with respect to the developments of the later theological debate.<br><br>However, while admitting all this, we believe that, while it would be appropriate to formulate certain expressions more appropriately and, perhaps, it would be desirable to add a few paragraphs, we cannot find anything better than the CFB1689 that expresses what we believe. There is no chapter or paragraph that we would like to eliminate and it, as a whole, represents "the things we believe with full certainty"<br>Street Address: <br>City: <br>State: <br>Country: <br>Location: <br>Service Times: <br>Phone: 0934 516 692<br>Pastor Name(s): Associated with Paul Washer, visitor<br>Website: www.solagrazia.it<br>Sermons: https://www.youtube.com/user/ccesgcl<br>Email: <br>Social Media: <br>Notes: <br><br><img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AL_Y2X6BVn2mEEypZfA50Xi5UQ8FPvsfb3RZQJyN7CwIB6L7Us0cB7bg-BPxUh6SVRpHvvjZY3fQZSrzMY-VGv6U4CZBgPyv3-HLasAPA9jqiDpgCPyhiFWdlIYBbjsryvouOj8u5xOyFGzX2mTc-X4mWRNzJyvV77IW3Rv-QskLMosb_qngjKAPtXszOUv1h-5TOu-6uOU?fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br><img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AL_Y2X5z82n9_VBbJSKPfN0JFtKPv-yfixtQTSqg_Z0ApQiEa0KvEheltGjXWr9OUsATaUmOq8SHaY3G-L4paSFWr6eOuulbyeHBQEHexywiuDZNqZHNAJwE6FyLEQMJQdB6bNQ22b3QqO4krLvy_ghb-yPYCxwtH2jjADROzXEYoRw11_xEcrFw4fpr9r-NWZTfk6IaFq4?fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br><img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AL_Y2X4kL0T90mOtIlOQg8mkbdhdwA7lrXjUgRvtwuyGKKDUgs0OnwW4ydA2Nf6TV-kRQxhPyj5-atQAbCEQzT88KBIHgJoTc6AeVpVywHA5SNL8BDPeJfupwD6IWxcPWVLuJ9O_gNO68b201Zimc63998tRim9K98LYu9g8xeAdAfVid6Uh6y9d9gHYqJfsxgyRNZ2nTB0?fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" />]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1697-DB4436</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Denomination">
            <value>Non-Denom</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Confessionalism">
            <value><![CDATA[1. The Baptist Confession of Faith of 1689
The Evangelical Christian Church Sola Grazia is a "confessional church". This means that it goes back and recognizes itself in historical Christianity which was expressed by compiling those compendia of the evangelical faith that flourished in the 16th and 17th centuries. In particular, the "Baptist Confession of Faith of 1689" (CFB1689) is the one that, in our opinion, better than all the others, contains the essence of biblical faith.

It is and remains a human and therefore fallible document. A document that was affected by the bitter polemics and theological discussions of its time and, therefore, more capable of responding to questions that we, today, would not put "on the agenda". Finally, being an "ancient" document, it is necessarily incomplete with respect to the developments of the later theological debate.

However, while admitting all this, we believe that, while it would be appropriate to formulate certain expressions more appropriately and, perhaps, it would be desirable to add a few paragraphs, we cannot find anything better than the CFB1689 that expresses what we believe. There is no chapter or paragraph that we would like to eliminate and it, as a whole, represents "the things we believe with full certainty"]]></value>
          </Data>
